libmpdclient: keep select()'s result, so EINTR is retried

In mpd_getNextReturnElement() the comparison was inside the assignment: err got
"select(...) == 1" (0 or 1), never select's -1, so "else if(err<0 && SELECT_ERRNO_IGNORE)
continue;" could not fire. A signal while waiting for MPD's reply (multimedia-daemon's
SIGCHLD when mplayer ends) was taken for a timeout, and the connection was dropped and made
again. The function's first select() already has the brackets right.

--- a/src/libmpdclient.c
+++ b/src/libmpdclient.c
@@ -596,7 +596,7 @@
 		tv.tv_usec = connection->timeout.tv_usec;
 		FD_ZERO(&fds);
 		FD_SET(connection->sock,&fds);
-		if((err = select(connection->sock+1,&fds,NULL,NULL,&tv) == 1)) {
+		if((err = select(connection->sock+1,&fds,NULL,NULL,&tv)) == 1) {
 			readed = recv(connection->sock,
 					connection->buffer+connection->buflen,
 					MPD_BUFFER_MAX_LENGTH-connection->buflen,
